Subject: [PATCH] Selected nodes filled and the Tab search's favourites,
 optionally like Nuke's

- nodeSelectedFill (Appearance > Node Graph; off by default): with a selected node tint above 0, a selected node is
  filled flat with the selection colour inside a thin rim (2.5 units) of its own shaded colour and keeps its usual
  outline, instead of being brightened with an outline in the selection colour.
- tabSearchNuke (Nodegraph; off by default, Natron's Tab search as before): the favourites (tabFavourites, the rows'
  text separated by |) listed first with a line under the last one; a star at each row's visible right end, filled
  for a favourite, that adds or removes one with a click (saved with the preferences; the click doesn't make the
  node); a green dot growing with Natron's own count of the nodes made from the Tab search; the typed letters bold
  where the search found them.
- nodeGraphCtrlWheelZooms (Appearance > Node Graph; off by default, since .sng8): Ctrl+wheel over the node graph
  zooms like the wheel alone, as in Nuke's node graph, instead of enlarging the node last clicked (Natron's
  magnifier, which artists took for the node changing size).
- Every new preference is read by name, so Settings.h doesn't change.

Core patch 0008 of the BeeeFX fork (layer/patches/).

Gap: layer/GAPS.md, item 1 (Tab node search: favourites) and "Nuke's look and habits" (the selected node).
Size: 6 files, 193 lines added, 12 removed.
upstream: not offered (Baptiste: keep the fork private for now).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
